<title>SPAIN: Peru targets Spain in privatisation drive.</title>
<headline>Peru targets Spain in privatisation drive.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru presented on Wednesday a portfolio of 50 companies during a trip to Spain, to be privatised by the year 2000, in the hope of attracting Spanish funds.</p>
<p>&quot;We have come to promote the privatisations and the program of concesions,&quot; said Ernesto Mitsumatsu, executive director of Peru's Private Investment Commission.</p>
<p>Peru hopes that Spain, its most important foreign investor, will invest in the assorted companies from the energy, mining and agriculture sectors and will bid for a handful of public works projects which it also presented.</p>
<p>&quot;Spain is our natural partner and has been involved since the start of the privatisations,&quot; said Mitsumatsu.</p>
<p>Peru has already privatised 75 percent of the state firms which generated income of some $7 billion for the state.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
